-- A file beside a program's sourced C++ header whose name is a standard
-- header (here `tuple` and `vector`) must not replace that header in the
-- pool, while a header the sourced one includes by angle brackets from the
-- same directory (`<sibling.hpp>`) still resolves. The sibling also defines
-- `OK` and `ERR` as macros, as ncurses.h does; the pool's own code below the
-- user headers must not use those names.
module main (foo)

import root-cpp

source Cpp from "helpers.hpp" ("twice")
twice :: Int -> Int

foo :: Int -> (Int, [Int])
foo x = (twice x, [x, x])
